    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10344" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπερι-σπαστός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drawnthrough,</i> of cautery,
				<i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.42
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπάω</span></b> , <i>draw
				off, divert,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.37
			</span></i>; esp. as military term, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.24.8
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				670b10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>divert, distract,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑαυτὸν ἄβακι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					5.24
				</span></i>
			.</div>
